// REJECTS: style should not be provided with non-list service parameter
//
// `style = simple` on a `String` parameter. The grammar attaches serviceParameterStyle to
// EVERY parameter regardless of its type -- `serviceParameter : identifier COLON typeReference
// PAREN_OPEN serviceParameterInfo PAREN_CLOSE` with style and explode among the info fields --
// and the restriction to LIST-typed parameters lives only in ServiceStoreParseTreeWalker:294
// (and :300 for `explode`).
//
// The type is written `[Integer]` for a list and `String` for a scalar, so the constraint
// couples an optional modifier to the bracket form of a type reference two rules away. That
// is exactly why ../fixtures/t2-servicestore.pure puts `style`/`explode` on its
// `[Integer]` parameter and not on the `String` one -- the placement is forced, not stylistic.
//
// `enum` and `allowReserved` sit in the same info block and are NOT restricted this way, so a
// rewrite cannot simply move the whole block behind a list check either.
###ServiceStore
ServiceStore fixture::neg::StyleOnScalar
(
  Service GetEmployee
  (
    path: '/employees';
    method: GET;
    parameters:
    (
      region: String ( location = query, style = simple )
    );
    response: fixture::neg::Employee <- fixture::neg::Binding;
    security: [];
  )
)
